# OCR Output Rules (XspensesAI)

Applies to any work involving OCR, PDF parsing, statement summaries, transaction extraction, and Prime/Byte/Tag handoff output.

## Required headings

When summarizing OCR or PDF content, use these exact headings in order:

## Summary
## Key details
## Transactions (cleaned)
## Issues / Uncertain lines

## Content requirements

- Use bullets only unless the user explicitly asks for paragraphs.
- `## Summary`: 3-6 short, plain-language bullets.
- `## Key details`: include statement period, institution/card, account last-4 (if present), and totals only if visible.
- `## Transactions (cleaned)`: `YYYY-MM-DD | Merchant | Amount | Currency | Notes`
- Use `UNKNOWN-DATE` when date is missing.
- Use `UNKNOWN-MERCHANT` when merchant is unclear.
- Do not invent values; place uncertain items in `## Issues / Uncertain lines`.

## Privacy and safety

- Do NOT persist raw OCR text by default.
- Keep logs minimal and redacted.
- Gate debug OCR views behind local/dev flags.
